oups Workplace Rights Home Bard considers applications for posted positions only. If you are interested in a position, follow the application instructions listed on the individual job posting. Unsolicited resumes and applications are discarded after 30 days. Applications are reviewed by a search committee or hiring manager responsible for determining applicant eligibility for an open position based on posted job requirements. Due to the high volume of applications, we are unable to answer phone calls or emails regarding the status of your application. Applying through Interfolio Bard College uses Interfolio.com for the majority of faculty and staff searches. Interfolio does not charge for applications; follow the specific link within a job posting. The Support page will assist with specific questions. For assistance with reference letters, click on Information for Letter Writers. For additional help using Interfolio or to submit a general application, contact the Office of Human Resources at [email protected] . Current Job Openings Equal Opportunity Employer Equal Opportunity Employer × Equal Opportunity Employer Bard College is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, mental, or physical disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, familial status, veteran status, or genetic information. Bard is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for all individuals in employment practices, services, programs, and activities. Academic Positions Al-Quds Bard, Palestine English Language Instructor Part-Time Undergraduate Faculty - Core Division Part-Time Undergraduate Faculty - Humanities & Practicing Arts Division Part-Time Undergraduate Faculty - Social Sciences Division Bard Graduate Center Assistant Professor in Fashion, Dress, and Textiles of the Americas Bard Prison Initiative Faculty, Bard Prison Initiative